Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:03:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/21] gicv3: put shared interrupts in Group 1

The GICv3 path reused the GICv2 distributor setup, which leaves every SPI
in Group 0. With the system-register CPU interface Group 0 is signalled as
FIQ and only Group 1 is enabled, so no SPI was ever taken: on qemu-oneplus6
the touch attention line raised INTID 647 at the distributor while the CPU
never read ICC_IAR1. Assign all SPIs to Group 1, as Linux gic_dist_init
does; secure firmware keeps its own assignment because the registers are
RAZ/WI to the kernel there.

Agent: Cursor agent (EMU-TOUCH)
Model: Auto
Provider: Cursor
